---
import Stop from "../Stop.astro";
import Shot from "../Shot.astro";
---

<Stop id="publish" title="You choose what reaches the merge request" log="!142 4 of 6 posted">
  <Shot
    name="publish"
    height={1521}
    view={900}
    focus={0.72}
    alt="Findings for MR !142, each with its own Publish button: the ones already posted to the merge request are marked Published, the rest still wait for a decision."
    caption="Each finding is published on its own, or all at once."
  />
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Nothing is posted on its own. You tick the findings worth a reviewer's time, and each
        one becomes an inline discussion on its file and line in the MR. Findings that are
        already published are never posted twice, so you can come back later and publish more.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        If you want the comments to sound like you, save samples of your writing as a voice
        profile. 4R rewrites the summary and each finding in that voice, and you publish the
        rewritten card or the original, card by card.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Stop>

<style>
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
